WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:01.768
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.402
We are hanging out
with Vince Vaughn!

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.338
Come on, now.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.040
-I had this idea
for this game for you

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.707
'cause you've been
in so many great movies.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.209
Alright?
And I wanted to see that

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.844
if you're a big enough fan
of movies

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:15.047
that you can summarize a movie
in just five seconds.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:16.916
It's time for
"Five Second Summaries."

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.451
Here we go.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.885
-♪ One, two, three,
four, five seconds ♪

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:22.789
♪ Summaries ♪

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.290
-Now, here's how the game works.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.326
We'll be given
the name of a movie.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.927
It'll pop up
on your Zoom screen.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.429
And as soon as you see
the title in your prompter,

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:33.666
you will have five seconds
to describe the plot

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.569
the best way you can and try
to make me guess what it is.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.772
You can't use any words
in the title,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.773
actors' names, or catch phrases.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:43.042
You're just describing
the plot of the movie.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.911
Does that sound good?
-Okay. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.812
Let's give it a shot.
-Alright.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.848
You're my guest, Vince,
so, please, you're up first.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.983
Let's put five seconds
on the clock.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.386
Take a look at the movie
in your prompter.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.188
And whenever you're ready.
-Okay. Go.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:58.457
Haunted hotel. Family. Dad chops
down a door with an axe.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.526
-"Amityville Horror"?
No. Oh, no.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.994
The one with Jack Nicholson.
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.429
"The Shining." "The Shining."
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.298
-That's right. That's right.
-I'm allowed to beat --

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.700
I'm allowed to answer
longer than five seconds.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.702
-That was a broad --
That was a broad description.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.136
It could have been either one.

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:12.938
It was just a --
It was just a --

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:15.108
-Alright. Here we go.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.510
Can I have five seconds
on the clock?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.012
Oh, okay. Yep.

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:22.648
Okay. Ready? Go.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.285
-There's a guy
living in his basement.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.720
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.355
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.357
-A guy living in his basement.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.526
[ Laughter ]
I have no answer for this.

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:36.863
-That's not true. You have to
have an answer for it.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.799
There's a guy living
in his basement.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.934
-There's a guy,
and he's living in his basement.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.771
That's where he lives.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.140
That happened to be
a home for him.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.975
This is an under
five-second description

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:51.677
of a movie that one might know.

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:53.712
-Yeah, that is correct.
-And that description

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.548
is that there's a gentleman
living in his basement.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.649
That's the best description.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.050
That's the premise
that we're working with.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.819
We have five seconds
to answer this question.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.587
I hope that that's clear to you.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:05.258
I will say, um, although
he wasn't living in a basement,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.359
but he was sort of isolated.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.694
I'll say "Being There,"
for the buzz.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:09.862
[ Buzzer ]
-Mm, sorry.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.298
-Yeah, that's wrong.
-"Parasite."

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.033
-"Parasite"!

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.069
I sadly never saw "Parasite."

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.603
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.238
-Well, alright, there you go.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:22.308
-But you know what? I bet
it's a terrific description,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.876
and I'm going to take the full
blame

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.244
for "Parasite"
not being answered.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:26.712
-No, no, no, I think --

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:27.913
-Well, no, I am, because if
I would have seen "Parasite" --

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.748
-I just ruined the movie
for you, I think.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:32.584
-It was impossible
for me to get that correct,

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:33.986
and you deserved better, Jimmy.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.222
I feel like little Poco Bueno.
-See, that's unbelievable.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.690
See, that's unbelievable.
That's the kind of --

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.658
He gives, and he gives,
and he gives.

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:41.627
-Guess what?
Sometimes you start slow,

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.129
but it's not over.
Tomorrow's a new day.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.564
Let's go. Three seconds.
Here we go.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.299
-We're making it
a little tighter.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.533
Three seconds on the clock.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:48.601
Vince Vaughn is up.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.271
Vince, whenever you're ready,
say "Go."

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:54.907
-Go. Giant ape royalty
fights giant lizard.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.509
-"Godzilla vs. Kong."
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.177
[ Bell dings ]

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.913
Wow! That was so fast!

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.214
-That was right.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:05.117
This is the comeback.
This is how we spell redemption.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.520
-Alright. Here we go. I got
three seconds for this one?

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.722
Oh, no, no.
-Hopefully I've seen it.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.858
-Yeah, I know. I don't know.
Alright, ready? Here we go.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.759
-Here we go.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:14.827
-Go.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.929
White fisherman's sweater.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:17.930
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.265
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:23.402
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.038
-Fisherman's sweater?

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.539
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.474
Yes.
-It's a sweater of a fisherman,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.509
and the color of this sweater
happens to be white.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:33.379
-Yep. Kind of stole the movie
a little bit.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:37.716
-I think once again, you've
given a terrific, terrific,

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:38.951
terrific --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.786
-You think so?
-Terrific --

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.021
I think you given
a terrific thing,

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:45.891
but I'm afraid
I may not have seen this movie.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.393
I might have been in my library

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.362
